Classify the query point $q=(2,2)$ using k-NN with $k=3$.

\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{align*}
d(q,P_1) &= \sqrt{1+1} = \sqrt{2} \approx 1.414 \\
d(q,P_2) &= \sqrt{0+1} = 1 \\
d(q,P_3) &= \sqrt{1+0} = 1 \\
d(q,P_4) &= \sqrt{16+16} \approx 5.657 \\
d(q,P_5) &= \sqrt{25+16} \approx 6.403
\end{align*}
Sorted by distance: $P_2(1), P_3(1), P_1(1.414), P_4(5.657), P_5(6.403)$. The 3 nearest neighbors are $P_2, P_3, P_1$ — all class A.
\boxed{\text{Predicted class} = A}

Using the same dataset as Example 3.22, classify $q=(6,5)$ using k-NN with $k=1$.

\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{align*}
d(q,P_1) &= \sqrt{25+16} \approx 6.403 \\
d(q,P_2) &= \sqrt{16+16} \approx 5.657 \\
d(q,P_3) &= \sqrt{25+9} \approx 5.831 \\
d(q,P_4) &= \sqrt{0+1} = 1 \\
d(q,P_5) &= \sqrt{1+1} \approx 1.414
\end{align*}
The single nearest neighbor is $P_4$ (distance $1$), which is class B.
\boxed{\text{Predicted class} = B}

