Classify the query point $q=(3.5,1.5)$ using k-NN with $k=4$.

\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{align*}
d(q,P_1) &= \sqrt{6.25+0.25} = \sqrt{6.5} \approx 2.550 \\
d(q,P_2) &= \sqrt{2.25+0.25} = \sqrt{2.5} \approx 1.581 \\
d(q,P_3) &= \sqrt{2.25+0.25} = \sqrt{2.5} \approx 1.581 \\
d(q,P_4) &= \sqrt{6.25+0.25} = \sqrt{6.5} \approx 2.550
\end{align*}
With $k=4$, all four points are neighbors: 2 of class A ($P_1,P_2$) and 2 of class B ($P_3,P_4$) — an exact tie.
\boxed{\text{Tie between A and B: an odd } k \text{ (e.g. } k=3\text{) should be used instead to avoid this}}
This illustrates exactly why $k$ is usually chosen to be odd for two-class problems, so majority voting cannot tie. \checkmark
